From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the copy engine's scratch never ends the session: a copy whose read or write scratch cannot grow goes through in stripes (always on); EDEN_UP_DMA_SCRATCH_MIB reserves both at the first launch (off)

T178a. T175 C3 died at the load from the field: std::bad_alloc from an 8,294,400-byte growth of
MaxwellDMA's read scratch on GPUBack (CopyBlockLinearToPitch -> GuestMemory::Read ->
ScratchBuffer::resize_destructive), caught by nothing; C1 lived through a failed 10,616,832-byte
one. run1419's heap site table shows the same site at 8 MiB.

Always on (a pure crash fix: it runs only where the std::bad_alloc used to end the session): the
three block-linear copies (block to pitch, pitch to block, block to block) catch std::bad_alloc
from their scratch and do the copy again in stripes through fixed buffers (3 x 128 KiB, .bss, one
copy at a time under a lock): per GOB row (8 lines), each GOB of the block-linear side (512 bytes)
read into a compact copy laid out as a one-GOB-tall surface of the same width, the same
SwizzleSubrect/UnswizzleSubrect run on it (block height and depth 0, origin y within the GOB), and
the GOBs written back with WriteBlockCached; the pitch side in the same lines. The reads are
ReadBlock where the whole copy read Safe and ReadBlockUnsafe where Unsafe, so the bytes that land
are the bytes the whole copy would have written (the whole copy also wrote back unchanged bytes
around the rectangle; the stripes leave those alone). Not the same: a copy whose source and
destination overlap (the whole copy read all of the source first). Shapes not covered rethrow, so
the session ends as before: lines past slice 0, a row wider than 16 KiB (4096 32-bit pixels; a
2304-wide one is 9 KiB), a row past the surface's GOBs, a pitch under a row or over 128 KiB, a block
to block copy with fewer source than destination lines. Each striped copy prints
EDEN_UP_DMA_STRIPE on stderr (the first 8, then at most one a second, with the counts); a shape
not covered prints it too ("rethrown"). Nothing is caught when the scratch grows: the hot path is
the same code inside a try.

EDEN_UP_DMA_SCRATCH_MIB=<MiB> (1-256; off unset): each DMA engine reserves its read and write
scratch at its first launch (one stderr line). 11 covers one 2304x1152 surface of 32-bit pixels
(10,616,832 bytes). Off by default: it costs 2 x the size per engine that copies, from its first
launch on, where today the scratch only holds what the copies asked for so far (it keeps the
largest anyway: resize_destructive only grows). With EDEN_AREA_CHANGE_SCRATCH_RELEASE=1 a growth
past the reserve still releases it first.

maxwell_dma.cpp/.h are not translation id inputs and no name is added to TranslationSwitches:
KEEPS THE STORE. Not checked on the console: the stripes have not run there; the byte equality is
read from SwizzleSubrectImpl (offset_y/offset_x/NativeGobOffset keep every byte of a GOB in its
GOB, and a GOB's place is (gob_y >> bh) * block_size + (gob_y & mask) << 9 + gob_x << x_shift).

